On Thu, May 7, 2009 at 12:18 PM, Michael Turniansky
<mturniansky@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> (In addition to xorxes' notation that "skarpinku" doesn't work,
> because it's in lujvo form,

More precisely, it's in slinku'i form. What I said is that
"loskarpinku" is a lujvo. "skarpinku" itself is a Lojban non-word, and
so it can't even be quoted with "zo".

> but "rp" is forbidden

Actually "r" is allowed next to any consonant but "r" itself, e.g.
"terpa", "zirpu".

> (I assume you meant "skarnpinku"

Yes, that would be a valid type-3 form. Sometimes people think the
recipe for type-3 fu'ivla is just rafsi+R+rest, but it is not just
that. The classifier rafsi has to end in a consonant (CCVC-, CVCC- or
CVC-), and the rest has to begin with a consonant (-C...V).

mu'o mi'e xorxes


